            "review_title": "Review at Viet Cuisine - Vietnamese Restaurant/ Vietnamese Cuisine",
            "review_text": "Vietcuisine - Taste of Viet\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam27 contributions\n0\n🌟 A Must-Try Spot in Phu My Hung – Viet Cuisine Review 🌟\nJul 2025 • Friends\nDuring my trip to Ho Chi Minh City, I visited Viet Cuisine in Phu My Hung, and it was honestly one of the best food experiences I had! The traditional Vietnamese interior is not only beautiful but also perfect for Instagram-worthy photos 📸\n\nThe food is fresh, light, and healthy – just right for Korean taste. I tried the bún thịt nướng and bánh xèo, and both were super flavorful. The dipping sauce (nước mắm) reminded me of Korean BBQ sauce, sweet and tangy. The gỏi cuốn (fresh spring rolls) felt familiar too, kind of like Korean ssam.\n\nThey have a Korean menu, the staff are friendly, and ordering was really easy. Even if you're short on time, you can order delivery through Delivery K!\n\nBonus tip: If you eat here 10 times, you can get a free ao dai (Vietnamese traditional dress)! 🎁 Sounds like a joke, but it’s real!\n\nWhether you're a tourist or living in Saigon, this is a spot you don’t want to miss. It's not just for visitors – locals love it too!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 8, 2025",
